      "writtenOn": "2019-09-27T18:45:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Needs clarification about access semantics.\n\nSometimes the metadata needs to be read before a fence has signaled. Eg. The display driver may need metadata information. Userspace wants to send that info to the kernel before the fence has signaled for performance reasons.\n\nTwo current proposals:\n1) Clarify when a buffer \"leaves\" a producer process, the producer should no longer attempt to write to the metadata. This needs to be carefully defined because buffers rarely actually leave a producer process. The leave is more logical (eg. queueBuffer in BufferQueue).\n\n2) [ARM proposal] \"lock()\" and \"unlock()\" functions for the metadata. In this case lock and unlock are meant as access control operations similar to a mutex not Mapper\u0027s usual lock and unlock operations. It would be on the vendor to implement probably through shared memory atomic primitives. Although c++ might not require the shared atomic primitives work.\n\nMaybe we can do a hybrid where we supply the \"lock()\" and \"unlock()\" and also add the option 1 clarification so vendors can use either?",
      "revId": "cc72fe32fc536152ad9fd57641c7b0a395ee80e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ce70df5_23ff4578",
        "filename": "graphics/mapper/4.0/IMapper.hal",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1468456
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-27T19:11:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the proposed lock/unlock would be across processes?",
      "parentUuid": "ade15aa9_5e37ee28",
      "revId": "cc72fe32fc536152ad9fd57641c7b0a395ee80e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a50609e_8c407502",
        "filename": "graphics/mapper/4.0/IMapper.hal",
